Nuxel USB-NET: own the Samsung NCM mirrorlink singleton exactly once.

With CONFIG_USB_ANDROID_SAMSUNG_COMPOSITE=y the pinned 4.14.253 vendor tree
registers a global misc device (usb_ncm / mirrorlink) and schedules a global
work item from ncm_alloc(), i.e. again for every bind, and frees both from
ncm_free_inst() with an unconditional misc_deregister().  The recorded pstore
panic (configfs rmdir -> ncm_attr_release -> ncm_free_inst -> misc_deregister)
is the result of that lifecycle:

  * register/deregister are unbalanced across binds and instances;
  * a failed misc_register() was reported as success and later deregistered;
  * ncm_work() dereferences mirrorlink_device.this_device, which is NULL
    between deregistration and the next registration, and _ncm_dev can be
    freed while the work is still queued (set_ncm_ready() races configfs
    teardown);
  * a second function instance can deregister the device the first still
    owns.

Fix: the misc device + work are one singleton owned by the set of live NCM
function instances.  mirrorlink_users is taken under mirrorlink_lock before
registration; later instances only take a reference.  ncm_function_cleanup()
prepares the final teardown under the lock (mirrorlink_active = false,
_ncm_dev = NULL), waits for in-flight ncm_alloc()/ncm_free() callers
(mirrorlink_refs), drains the work with cancel_work_sync(), removes the fix
attribute and performs exactly one misc_deregister().  Register and deregister
run without the spinlock (they sleep) but under mirrorlink_txn so they can
never interleave.  ncm_work() and set_ncm_ready() re-check mirrorlink_active
under the lock.  ncm_alloc() propagates registration failure (ERR_PTR) and
undoes refcnt/kfree.  Module exit releases the singleton even when no function
instance remains.

The module also exports const char nuxel_ncm_lifecycle_marker[] =
"nuxel-ncm-lifecycle-fix-v2" and the misc device exposes
/sys/class/misc/usb_ncm/nuxel_fix with the same value, so build/CI tooling can
prove the RUNNING image carries the fix without creating a gadget first.  Userspace (tools/beta/live/nuxel-usb-net.py and
services/nuxel-s10/bin/nuxel-usb-net-helper.sh) refuses to create an NCM
function unless this marker is present, so the RUNNING kernel - not the
4.14.253 version string - decides whether NCM may be used.

--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
